<section class="phero"><img class="phero-bg" src="/assets/img/photos/rochester.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/rochester-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/rochester.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="768" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><div class="phero-shade"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/where-we-appraise/">Locations</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Rochester</span></nav><p class="kicker">Finger Lakes</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Rochester, New York</h1><p class="lede">An insurance appraiser in Rochester sees ice, wind and water claims on some of the most character-rich older homes in upstate New York. We help Monroe County owners reach a fair amount of loss when the insurer’s estimate falls short.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-orange" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-l" href="/reach-us/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Monroe County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Finger Lakes</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<div class="local-card"><div><p class="lc-t">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips"><li>Ice storms</li><li>Lake-effect snow &amp; ice dams</li><li>High wind &amp; tree fall</li><li>Frozen &amp; burst pipes</li><li>Lakeshore flooding (flood)</li></ul></div><div><p class="lc-t">Housing mix</p><p>Rochester’s housing is largely early 20th-century wood-frame singles and doubles, Victorians and Colonial Revivals, with mid-century homes in the surrounding towns.</p></div><div><p class="lc-t">Areas we visit</p><p>Park Avenue, South Wedge, Corn Hill, Highland Park, Browncroft, Charlotte, Nineteenth Ward, North Winton Village</p></div></div>

<h2>From the 1991 ice storm to the lakeshore</h2>
<p>Many Rochester residents remember the March 1991 ice storm, which coated the region in heavy ice, brought down trees and power lines across Monroe County and left large parts of the area without power for days. Winters still bring lake-effect snow, ice dams and frozen pipes. Along Lake Ontario, record-high water levels in 2017 and again in 2019 caused shoreline flooding and erosion in towns such as Greece, Hamlin and Irondequoit. Rising lake water and erosion are generally excluded from homeowners policies, but wind and ice damage to the same homes may be covered.</p>
<h2>Victorian detail meets the estimate</h2>
<p>Park Avenue, Corn Hill, the South Wedge and the Nineteenth Ward hold large stocks of Victorians, foursquares and Arts and Crafts homes with wood clapboard, decorative trim, plaster walls and original hardwood. Browncroft and Highland Park add Tudors and Colonial Revivals with slate or tile roofs. These materials are expensive to match and repair, and insurers sometimes scope them as if the house were built last year.</p>
<h2>Frequent Monroe County disputes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Tree damage to roofs and framing priced as surface repairs.</li>
<li>Ice-dam water damage called long-term leakage.</li>
<li>Wood siding and trim scoped as vinyl replacements.</li>
<li>Shoreline homes where wind damage and lake flooding overlap.</li>
<li>Code upgrades for knob-and-tube wiring or old framing omitted.</li>
</ul>
<p>Monroe County winters are also hard on plumbing in older homes, especially in kitchens and bathrooms built against exterior walls. When a pipe bursts while a home is vacant or during a cold snap, insurers sometimes question whether heat was maintained. That is a coverage question, but once coverage is accepted, the scope of drying, demolition and rebuild is often where the money is.</p><p>Illustrative example: if an insurer’s estimate replaces damaged clapboard on one wall with vinyl, and the rest of the house remains wood, the result neither matches nor reflects the home’s actual materials.</p>
<h2>Where we work around Rochester</h2>
<p>We cover the city, including Park Avenue, the South Wedge, Corn Hill, Highland Park, Browncroft, Charlotte, Maplewood, the Nineteenth Ward and North Winton Village, along with Brighton, Pittsford, Penfield, Webster, Irondequoit, Greece, Gates and Henrietta. If you are getting ready to invoke appraisal, our <a href="/appraisal-calculators/claim-calendar-builder/">claim calendar builder</a> helps you track policy deadlines, since many New York policies limit lawsuits to two years from the loss; check yours. To have us represent you on a panel, see <a href="/claim-appraisals/appraisal-panel-representation/">appraisal panel representation</a>.</p>

<h2>Appraisal services for Rochester properties</h2>
<p>Every New York Insurance Appraiser service is available in Rochester and across Monroe County, including:</p>
<ul class="cols"><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/appraisal-panel-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/homeowners-insurance-appraisal/">Homeowners Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/co-op-condo-commercial-appraisal/">Co-op, Condo &amp; Commercial Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/roof-hail-damage-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/">Windstorm &amp; Tornado Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/hurricane-noreaster-appraisal/">Hurricane &amp; Nor’easter Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/burst-pipe-water-damage-appraisal/">Water Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/fire-smoke-damage-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Rochester claim questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>My lakeshore home has wind and flood damage. How is that handled?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Usually as separate claims. Wind and ice damage may fall under your homeowners policy, while flooding from rising lake water is generally excluded and handled under flood insurance if you have it. Separate scopes help keep each claim accurate.</p></div></details><details><summary>How long do I have to invoke appraisal?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>It depends on your policy. Many New York policies limit lawsuits to two years from the date of loss, and appraisal can take time, so starting early is wise. Check your policy or ask a New York attorney.</p></div></details></div>
